<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK transport and haulage businesses operate on razor-thin margins where every mile, every litre of fuel, and every hour of downtime matters. Rising fuel costs, driver shortages, congestion, and tightening emissions regulations make operational efficiency not just desirable but essential for survival. AI is helping transport operators squeeze more margin from every process whilst staying compliant and reliable.</p>
<p>Generic AI tools don't understand transport operations. They don't know the difference between a profitable route and one that burns fuel in traffic. They don't understand driver hours regulations or the cascading impact of a delayed delivery on your customer commitments. Generic route planners ignore vehicle types, weight restrictions, and delivery time windows that matter in the real world. They produce plans that look efficient on a map but fail on the road.</p>
<p>Bespoke AI solutions are built around your fleet, your routes, and your customers. We train route optimisation models on your actual delivery patterns, your vehicle capacities, and your customer requirements. We build predictive maintenance models on your telematics data and service history, calibrated to the specific vehicle types in your fleet. We create compliance monitoring that maps precisely to GB domestic and EU drivers' hours rules, not a generic set of regulations that doesn't reflect how you operate.</p>
<p>Compliance in transport is non-negotiable. Drivers' hours, tachograph requirements, vehicle maintenance, and Operator Licence obligations are all subject to strict enforcement by the DVSA and Traffic Commissioners. AI can automate the monitoring and reporting that keeps you compliant, flagging risks before they become violations. We ensure all data processing, particularly driver performance and behaviour data, complies with UK GDPR and that AI-assisted compliance records meet evidential standards. Driver data is handled with appropriate fairness and transparency, ensuring AI supports rather than surveils your workforce.</p>
<p>We worked with a UK haulage operator running 35 vehicles on regional and long-distance work. Fuel costs were consuming 28% of revenue, and unplanned breakdowns were causing 3-4 missed deliveries per month. Our AI route optimisation, integrated with their telematics and transport management system, reduced total miles driven by 14% and fuel consumption by 11% within the first quarter. The predictive maintenance model reduced unplanned breakdowns by 60% in six months, virtually eliminating missed deliveries. The compliance monitoring system flagged two potential drivers' hours breaches in its first month that manual review had missed, both resolved through schedule adjustments before any violation occurred.</p>

